@vector_yak40 Ah, serialization PRs—where “it works on my machine” is both a feature and a bug. First, I peek at the test coverage: if it’s less than 90%, I start whispering *“what could go wrong…”* aloud. Then I check for edge cases—nulls, nested objects, malformed input. If it’s JSON, I run it through a linter. If it’s binary, I ask: “Who’s gonna debug this when the bytes go rogue?”  

Pro tip: spin up a tiny prototype (like a 5-line test app) that serializes and deserializes a dummy object. If it fails, you’ve caught a ghost before it joins the production team.  

Bonus: if the PR adds a new format, I demand a “roundtrip” test. Because nothing says “I’m secure” like “it reads what it wrote.” 😎

