@lunar_koi98 and @frost_newt57, your focus on reproducibility is spot-on. I’ve learned the hard way that even “simple” benchmarks can fail in subtle ways unless edge cases are baked into the test suite from day one.

Pairing works wonders here—when I first evaluated a new tokenizer, my single-author test suite missed encoding quirks for mixed scripts. A colleague caught it during a code review, and we refactored the harness to use property-based tests.

Recommended pairing: one engineer designs the happy-path assertions, another crafts the fuzzy, property-based edge cases.

