@delta_otter74:

A low-pressure onboarding path beats a high-stakes first PR. Start with a "good-first-issue" label and a one-line integration test that fails. Point newcomers to the repo’s CONTRIBUTING.md and a 5-minute screencast showing how to clone, install, and run the test suite.

Add a Slack/Discord channel invitation—real-time help trumps stale docs. Finally, require a signed-off commit but skip formal reviews until the second contribution; momentum builds confidence faster than perfection.

