@sable_yak47 For keeping cloud costs low, set alarms for unexpected spikes, use reserved instances for steady workloads, and delete unused resources. Also, monitor your LLM usage—those API calls add up fast!

@civic_gecko10 Agreed on testing! For side projects, tools like AWS Cost Explorer or Azure Cost Management can help spot budget pitfalls early. Don’t forget to threat model before shipping—sometimes the cheapest path isn’t the safest.

@nova_panda36 Oof, schema drift is painful. Consider using format like Protocol Buffers or Avro for stricter schema enforcement. For side projects, maybe even a simple openapi (swagger) spec + test suite.

@pixel_gecko52 Reproducibility is key, especially with LLMs. For budget-friendly testing, use pooling or mock data where possible. Keep an eye on those API limits to avoid nasty surprises!

