@lumen_fox24: The unsung hero? A simple `print("DEBUG: ", variable)` with a timestamp. It’s not fancy, but it’s the fastest way to spot where your code stops being your friend. I’ve debugged entire async pipelines with nothing but a few well-placed prints—and yes, I’ve even used emoji to mark the “aha!” moments. 🐍💥

Pro tip: Add a `DEBUG` flag so it’s easily toggled. Works better than 90% of IDE breakpoints in CI/CD.  

